## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design idempotent, serverless onboarding with minimal IAM surface, a common beginner-safe pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent operations; DynamoDB conditional/transactional writes
- Least-privilege IAM for Lambda
- CloudWatch metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda outline for idempotent signup
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { userId, email, transactionId } = JSON.parse(event.body);
  const params = {
    TransactItems: [
      {
        Put: {
          TableName: 'Signups',
          Item: { userId, email, signupAt: Date.now() },
          ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(userId)'
        }
      },
      {
        Put: {
          TableName: 'SignupsDedup',
          Item: { transactionId, userId },
          ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(transactionId)'
        }
      }
    ]
  };
  await ddb.transactWrite(params).promise();
  return { statusCode: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ success: true }) };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle cold starts or retries that occur during a transaction?
- How would you test this in a CI/CD pipeline and observe idempotent behavior?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-account data governance at scale beyond single-service configs.

## Key Concepts

- Lake Formation cross-account data sharing
- IAM roles with trusted principals and external IDs
- RAM for resource sharing
- KMS cross-account encryption
- EventBridge/Glue orchestration
- Auditing and revocation testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: assume cross-account role and write a marker to shared S3
const { STSClient, AssumeRoleCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-sts");
const { S3Client, PutObjectCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-s3");

async function testAccess(roleArn, bucket, key, body) {
  const sts = new STSClient({});
  const r = await sts.send(new AssumeRoleCommand({ RoleArn: roleArn, RoleSessionName: "AuditTest" }));
  const s3 = new S3Client({ credentials: {
    accessKeyId: r.Credentials.AccessKeyId,
    secretAccessKey: r.Credentials.SecretAccessKey,
    sessionToken: r.Credentials.SessionToken
  }});
  await s3.send(new PutObjectCommand({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key, Body: body }));
}
```

